comparative data substantially formalizes the recently introduced Convergence Field Atlas. It distinguishes explicit, procedural, developmental, and evolutionary “knowing,” then treats repeated independent solutions as samples of a constrained search landscape:

possibility\ space
\rightarrow physical/developmental\ constraints
\rightarrow variation
\rightarrow selection
\rightarrow inheritance.

The key architectural move is to infer basins of attraction / constraint fields from repeated convergence rather than simply borrowing nature’s designs. 

power move introduces a proper Meta Ecology Observatory / Meta-Meta Engine. Instead of asking which strategy wins, it represents the ecology that makes a strategy viable:

M(t)=\{Rules,Components,Strategies,Frequencies,Payoffs,Information,Narrative,Economy\}

and tracks:

\Delta M=M(t+1)-M(t).

It explicitly models reflexivity: once agents know the meta, their behavior changes the meta; above the players sits the rule-maker who can alter the possibility space itself. 

three bins makes the Delta Observatory much more operational. Deltas are triaged into Noise, Drift, and Regime Change. Its governing criterion is whether resolving a discrepancy would change prediction, decision, or action; several individually insignificant deltas can accumulate into drift and eventually justify model replacement. 

reality gap names a useful general quantity: Ontic Delta, the discrepancy between a represented state and what actually exists. That nests prediction error, map–territory error, sim-to-real error, and implementation error under a common abstraction. 

implied leverage then adds an important second-order measure: surface magnitude and implication magnitude are different variables. A small observation can be high-value when it forces widespread belief revision; a dramatic event can be low-information if it changes no useful predictions. 

shared compressed context reframes common sense as unspoken shared state between agents. When that overlap cannot be assumed, the prescribed fallback is explicit definitions, observable evidence, constraints, prediction/feedback, and negotiated rules. The resulting rule is stronger than “use common sense”:

Do not assume common sense across an unverified boundary; establish shared sense first. 

self modeling of models adds an explicit inverse-rendering model of social selfhood: another agent does not observe your hidden state; it observes outputs and reconstructs the cheapest latent model capable of explaining them. Repeated mismatch eventually makes the current model more expensive than an alternative, producing nonlinear perspective flips. 

embodied semantics broadens meaning beyond symbols to position, timing, motion, scale, trajectory, constraint, and power. It also introduces a useful nested-game rule: competence includes detecting which game layer is actually active and whether another actor can escalate or rewrite the game. Dominance at one layer therefore cannot establish total power. 

pkl closes a complementary loop between tacit and explicit systems intelligence:

embodied\ intuition
\rightarrow invariant
\rightarrow explicit\ model
\rightarrow generalization

and back:

abstract\ model
\rightarrow action\ grammar
\rightarrow practice
\rightarrow procedural\ intuition.

That is effectively a bidirectional compiler between body and abstraction. 

Finally, escl formalizes the human–AI interface itself as an Externalized Second Cognitive Loop: externalization creates distance; distance permits alternative representations; a sufficiently different second loop can challenge and expand rather than simply echo. The artifact explicitly identifies the failure mode externalize → echo → intensify → repeat, which is important for Reality Stitch. 

